1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,150
2026年10月11日，利物浦安菲尔德
客场看台升起了数百根充气香蕉
Anfield, 11 October 2026. Hundreds of inflatable bananas rise in the away end.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:07,250
这是曼城被裁定114项指控成立后
踢的第一场比赛
City's first match since 114 charges against them were upheld.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,300
为什么偏偏是香蕉？
答案要回到39年前
Why bananas? The answer is 39 years old.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,700
1987年的曼彻斯特，工厂接连关门
曼城刚刚从顶级联赛降级
Manchester, 1987: the mills were closing, and City had just been relegated.

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:19,300
英格兰足球也在最灰暗的年代
看台围着铁丝网，球队被禁欧战
English football at its darkest: caged terraces, English clubs banned from Europe.

6
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,300
8月15日，曼城主场对普利茅斯
球迷弗兰克·牛顿扛来一根大香蕉
15 August, v Plymouth: fan Frank Newton carries in a giant inflatable banana.

7
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:26,250
这根充气香蕉有1.7米长
没人知道为什么，大家都笑了
Five feet six of inflatable fruit. Nobody knew why. Everybody laughed.

8
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:30,800
到赛季末，球迷把前锋瓦拉迪
唱成了“伊姆雷·香蕉”
By season's end, striker Imre Varadi had become 'Imre Banana' in the chants.

9
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:34,950
最后一个客场，已有约50根香蕉
下个赛季，鲨鱼、鳄鱼、恐龙也来了
By the last away game there were about fifty. Next season: sharks, crocodiles, dinosaurs.

10
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:39,050
香蕉厂商加大了产量
还有水果公司开始赞助曼城的比赛
A banana maker stepped up production. A fruit company sponsored City games.

11
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:43,250
同一时期，曼彻斯特的夜店
响起了迷幻浩室音乐
Meanwhile, Manchester's clubs were playing acid house.

12
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:45,400
一座萧条的城市
在找自己的快乐
A city in decline, finding its own joy.

13
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:49,500
1988年节礼日，客场斯托克城
一万两千名曼城球迷奇装异服来了
Boxing Day 1988, away at Stoke: 12,000 City fans in fancy dress.

14
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:53,000
主队让出了整整两面看台
球员们也抱着充气玩具出场
Stoke gave them two whole sides of the ground. The players ran out with inflatables too.

15
00:00:53,150 --> 00:00:56,300
那天曼城输了
比分没人记得，大家只记得香蕉
City lost. Nobody remembers the score. Everyone remembers the bananas.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,700
后来，球场改成全座席
充气玩具渐渐消失，曼城却一路下滑
Then came all-seater grounds. The inflatables faded; City kept falling.

17
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:04,300
1998年，曼城跌入第三级别
这是球队从未到过的最低谷
1998: down to the third tier, lower than City had ever been.

18
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:09,200
1999年附加赛决赛，第89分钟
曼城还0比2落后
1999 play-off final at Wembley: 89 minutes gone, City 2-0 down.

19
00:01:09,450 --> 00:01:14,250
补时阶段扳平比分
点球大战，他们赢了
Level in stoppage time. Then they won on penalties.

20
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:18,300
2008年，阿布扎比财团收购曼城
冠军开始一座接一座
2008: Abu Dhabi buys the club. The trophies start arriving.

21
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:22,300
2012年，44年来首个顶级联赛冠军
2023年，三冠王
2012: first league title in 44 years. 2023: the treble.

22
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,200
同一年，英超提出115项指控
查的正是夺冠那些年的账
Same year: 115 Premier League charges, covering the years of those titles.

23
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:29,600
官司打了三年多
香蕉静静躺在老球迷的鞋盒里
The case ran for more than three years. The bananas lay in old fans' shoeboxes.

24
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:32,950
2026年9月29日
独立委员会作出裁决
29 September 2026: the independent commission rules.

25
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:37,600
115项指控中，114项成立
处罚未定，曼城否认违规并已上诉
114 of 115 charges upheld. Sanctions pending; City deny wrongdoing and have appealed.

26
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:42,850
于是，香蕉回来了。曼城3比0取胜
“这群球迷，一直在坐过山车”
So the bananas came back, and City won 3-0. 1894: 'This fan base has always been on a rollercoaster.'

27
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
主队看台的横幅写着：
“一代球迷被欺骗了”
The home end's banner: 'A generation of supporters cheated.'

28
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:50,800
也有人说，这些香蕉
成了俱乐部的挡箭牌
Others say the bananas have become the club's shield.

29
00:01:51,450 --> 00:01:54,900
可香蕉诞生的那年
曼城一无所有，只有球迷
But when the banana was born, City had nothing but their fans.

30
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:59,550
账本上的对错，交给裁决
举起香蕉的球迷，没有做错什么
Let the verdict judge the accounts. The fans holding bananas did nothing wrong.

31
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,150
跌到第三级别时，他们在
When City fell to the third tier, they were there.

32
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:04,600
站上欧洲之巅时，他们也在
When City stood on top of Europe, they were there too.

33
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:10,500
香蕉没变
举香蕉的人，一直都在
The banana hasn't changed. The people holding it never left.
